course: dictionary
lesson: 8713
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The clues in the sentence show which meaning the writer means. Senseless is one of these words. «The senseless waste of food shocked everyone.» Waste is the clue: nothing good came from it, so senseless means pointless and foolish.
explain: «The boxer was knocked senseless in the third round.» Knocked is the clue. Senseless here means unconscious, not able to feel or know what is happening. Same word, different meaning.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Try your meaning in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have found it. If not, try the other meaning. A dictionary lists each meaning with a number so you can check.
fact: Senseless means without meaning or good reason, foolish and pointless.
fact: Senseless also means unconscious, not able to feel or know what is happening.
fact: «Senseless violence» means cruel harm that has no good reason behind it.
fact: «A senseless waste» means something valuable thrown away for nothing.
fact: «Knocked senseless» means knocked unconscious.
exercise: «The senseless waste of paper upset the whole class.» What does senseless mean here? | Unconscious | Full of meaning | Very quiet | *Pointless and foolish
exercise: «He was knocked senseless when he fell off the wall.» What does senseless mean here? | Angry | Foolish and pointless | Happy and laughing | *Unconscious
exercise: Which sentence uses senseless to mean unconscious? | «It was senseless to run out in the storm.» | «The senseless violence shocked the town.» | *«The blow left him senseless on the ground.» | «She made a senseless joke.»
test: Which meaning fits «a senseless waste of time»? | Very loud | Unconscious | Hard to see | *Pointless and foolish
test: Which meaning fits «the boxer lay senseless on the mat»? | Lost in thought | Foolish and pointless | *Unconscious | Happy
exam: What is the difference between «senseless violence» and «knocked senseless»? | *The first means cruel and pointless, the second means unconscious | Neither has a meaning | The first means unconscious, the second means cruel and pointless | Both mean exactly the same
